      "writtenOn": "2023-11-16T09:53:34Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "In the original design, ChannelSoundingSingleSideData has a variable running_tone_pct with is a three-dimensional array (std::vector\u003cstd::vector\u003cstd::vector\u003cstd::complex\u003cdouble\u003e\u003e\u003e\u003e). It is a buffer that stores the previous procedures\u0027 tone_pct, including aborted subevents.\n\nAIDL doesn\u0027t support multi-dimensional arrays with dynamic size, so we need to create another Parcelable object for this. Moreover, the Bluetooth stack needs to create a buffer for this data and send it to HAL, with most of the data being duplicates.\n\nAfter discussing with the Tech Eng team, we concluded that sending abort event data to the HAL would eliminate the need for the aforementioned efforts. The HAL would be responsible for buffering the event data, and a boolean flag should be implemented to allow the HAL to determine whether abort event data is required for tuning the ranging algorithm.\n\nThis also benefit for running_step_channels.\nThanks!",
      "parentUuid": "8a2f7c20_002fedcb",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 70,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 77,
        "endChar": 41
      },
